body:
### Does this issue occur when all extensions are disabled?

Not applicable — this is in `runInTerminalTool` / `chatServiceImpl` in VS Code core, with a contributing short-circuit in the bundled Copilot Chat prompt renderer.

### Version

Broken: 1.131.0 (Copilot Chat 0.59.0)
Last known good: 1.127.0 (Copilot Chat 0.55.0)

### Steps to Reproduce

1. In agent mode, start a long-running background terminal command that outlives the turn (e.g. `gh pr checks <n> --watch`).
2. Let the turn end while the command is still running. (Sleeping the machine makes this reliable, but sleep is not required — any command finishing after the turn ends will do.)
3. When the command completes, VS Code auto-sends a system-initiated chat request:

```js
// RunInTerminalTool, onCommandFinished
this._chatService.sendRequest(sessionId,
  `[Terminal ${t} notification: command completed${exit}. …]\nTerminal output:\n${out}`,
  { ...opts, queue: "steering", isSystemInitiated: true, terminalExecutionId: t })
```

4. The model replies as if it has no context — e.g. "I'm ready to help — what would you like me to work on?" — and any repo instructions, `AGENTS.md`, and skills are absent for that turn.

### What happens

That auto-sent turn is built **without instructions and without the automatic-context pass**. Prompt-token composition from one session, three consecutive requests:

| request | type | promptTokens | composition |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | user message | 152,632 | System 23% · Tools 68% · Messages 8% · ToolResults 3% |
| 3 | terminal-completion (`isSystemInitiated=true`) | **29,520** | Tools 95% · Messages 5% · **System 0%** |
| 4 | user message | 177,124 | normal |

~29K is tool definitions only. Request 4 shows conversation history was never actually lost — only that one turn was blind.

The persisted transcript shows the system-initiated request carrying `variableData: { variables: [] }`, while the turns on either side carry `copilot-instructions.md` and `AGENTS.md` as `automaticallyAdded` promptFiles.

### Root cause

`runInTerminalTool.ts` captures only four fields when registering the background-completion notification:

```ts
// src/vs/workbench/contrib/terminalContrib/chatAgentTools/browser/tools/runInTerminalTool.ts:3035
const sendOptions: { userSelectedModelId?, modeInfo?, userSelectedTools?, agentIdSilent? } = {};
if (lastRequest) {
    sendOptions.userSelectedModelId = lastRequest.modelId;
    sendOptions.modeInfo            = lastRequest.modeInfo;
    sendOptions.agentIdSilent       = lastRequest.response?.agent?.id;
    sendOptions.userSelectedTools   = constObservable(lastRequest.userSelectedTools);
}
```

`instructionContext` is not among them. The chat service then bails out early:

```ts
// chatServiceImpl.ts:1490
const collectInstructions = async () => {
    const ctx = options?.instructionContext;
    if (!ctx) { return []; }   // ← whole ComputeAutomaticInstructions pass skipped
```

So no `copilot-instructions.md`, no `AGENTS.md`, no `.instructions.md`, no skills catalog for that request.

This compounds with an intentional short-circuit in the Copilot Chat prompt renderer, which also drops the environment/context body for system-initiated turns:

```js
if (this.props.isSystemInitiated) return <UserMessage>{this.props.request}</UserMessage>;
```

Net result: the model receives a bare `[Terminal … completed]` string.

### Regression range

Scanned persisted sessions for system-initiated turns:

| date | version | promptTokens | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2026-07-20 | 1.127.0 / copilot 0.55.0 | 247,512 (Messages 18%) | fine |
| 2026-07-28 | 1.127.0 / 0.55.0 | 171,125 (Messages 15%) | fine |
| 2026-07-30 | 1.127.0 / 0.55.0 | 387,255 (Messages 36%) | fine — fired 33h after the turn ended |
| 2026-08-10 | 1.131.0 / 0.59.0 | not recorded | broken |
| 2026-08-11 | 1.131.0 / 0.59.0 | 29,520 | broken |

Points to **1.131.0 / Copilot Chat 0.59.0**.

### Suggested fix

Pass `instructionContext` through, mirroring what `chatWidget.ts:2884` does for user-initiated turns:

```ts
const sendOptions: {
    userSelectedModelId?: string;
    modeInfo?: IChatRequestModeInfo;
    userSelectedTools?: IObservable<UserSelectedTools>;
    agentIdSilent?: string;
    instructionContext?: IChatSendRequestOptions['instructionContext'];
} = {};
if (lastRequest) {
    …
    // Without this the notification turn runs with no instructions/skills attached.
    sendOptions.instructionContext = {
        modeKind: lastRequest.modeInfo?.kind ?? ChatModeKind.Agent,
        enabledTools: lastRequest.userSelectedTools,
    };
}
```

One change covers all three call sites (input-needed :3160, completed :3216, terminal-exited :3291) since they all spread `sendOptions`.

Whether the `isSystemInitiated` renderer short-circuit should also be relaxed is a separate judgement call for the Copilot Chat side — fixing `instructionContext` alone restores instructions and skills, which is the bulk of the loss.

### Existing issues checked

Searched `microsoft/vscode` and `microsoft/vscode-copilot-release`; nothing appears to track this mechanism.

- `microsoft/vscode#328533` — missing confirmation for subagent tool after steering (open, different)
- `microsoft/vscode#327607`, `#326244`, `#327387` — other steering-message bugs, all closed pre-1.131
- `vscode-copilot-release#14145` — generic "loses earlier chat context" umbrella, no mechanism identified

### Workaround

Run long pollers (`--watch` and similar) synchronously so they complete inside the turn, or simply re-prompt afterwards — the conversation history is intact; only the auto-sent turn is affected.

Happy to open a PR with the change above if maintainers agree with the direction.
